    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d417">

                <pb facs="0582" n="476" sameAs="frus:frus1906p1/pg476"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Chargé Sleeper to the Secretary of State</hi>.</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram—Paraphrase.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >American Legation, Habana</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1906-09-12"><hi rendition="#italic">September
                                12, 1906</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>(Mr. Sleeper reports that in a short conversation with the President that
                    afternoon he urged American citizens and interests be furnished <pb facs="0583"
                        n="477" xml:id="pg477"/> all protection possible, and says that many
                    Americans have complained to legation that the protection already requested has
                    not been afforded. In reply to an inquiry as to ability of Government to crush
                    rebellion he replied evasively.)</p>
                <p>(Mr. Sleeper announces arrival of the cruiser <hi rendition="#italic"
                    >Denver</hi>, and asks full instructions.)</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
